<title>FRANCE: French unemployment rises 32,400 in May.</title>
<headline>French unemployment rises 32,400 in May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French unemployment jumped 1.1 percent in May, reversing three months of declines, figures released on Monday by the employment ministry showed.</p>
<p>The official jobless number climbed 32,400 to 3,113,500, delivering a stark reminder to France's new Socialist-led government of the uphill task it faces in fulfilling its election pledge to cut unemployment.</p>
<p>The unemployment rate, calculated according to International Labour Organisation standards, remained unchanged at 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-May   month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.5 pct   0.0 pctge pt   0.2 pctge pt</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,113,500     1.1 pct	    2.3 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	3,205,000     0.5 pct	    2.0 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  212,200     0.6 pct	   13.8 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 368,300    -6.6 pct	   -2.6 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    344,100    -3.7 pct	   -2.7 pct</p>
